"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[27453],{327453:(e,s,t)=>{t.r(s),t.d(s,{default:()=>n});let n="# Retrieving MLflow Traces\n\nSearch and filter traces using the `search_traces` tool. The experiment ID is automatically available from page context.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Clarify what the user is looking for: by status, time range, user, session, name, or assessment.\n2. Build a filter expression using the `search_traces` tool. See [`filter-reference.md`](filter-reference.md) for syntax.\n3. Analyze results: count matches, check status distribution, identify patterns (error clustering, latency outliers).\n4. For interesting traces, use `get_trace` to examine the full span tree.\n\n## Common Queries\n\n- Recent errors: `status = 'ERROR'`\n- By user: `metadata.\\`mlflow.trace.user\\` = 'user@example.com'`\n- By session: `metadata.\\`mlflow.trace.session\\` = 'session-123'`\n- By name: `name LIKE '%chat%'` (case-sensitive) or `name ILIKE '%chat%'` (case-insensitive)\n- Slow traces: `execution_time_ms > 5000`\n- By span type: `span.type = 'LLM'`\n- By span name: `span.name LIKE '%retriever%'`\n- Combine: `status = 'ERROR' AND name = 'my_chain'`\n- Combine with span: `span.type = 'LLM' AND execution_time_ms > 3000`\n\n**Note**: Filtering by assessment values (feedback/expectation) is NOT supported. Use `get_assessments` on individual traces instead.\n"}}]);
